<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef uneven on light to moderate demand and offerings.  Select rib, chuck and round cuts weak while the Choice rib, chuck, round and loin steady to firm. Beef trimmings generally steady on light to moderate demand and offerings. - USDA</p>
<p>------</p>
<p>243 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p> 14 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>17 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     102.67	103.09	 97.99	 97.53</p>
<p>Changes	   0.57	  0.45	 -0.14	 -0.11</p>
<p>Rib	  162.84	160.82	155.29	154.47</p>
<p>Chuck	 70.12	 71.35	 72.71	 70.65</p>
<p>Round	 87.90	 87.90	 86.26	 86.26</p>
<p>Loin	 160.99	162.34	141.07	142.25</p>
<p>Brisket     63.55	 63.55	 62.14	 62.14</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  68.15	 68.06	 68.38	 68.20</p>
<p>Flank	 58.35	 58.35	 59.18	 59.18</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
